  <prompt>
    Wire the enrichment assessment (task 010's `ICommunicationEnrichmentService`) to fire `EventRulesService.FireAsync("communication_assessed")`, which drives ordered Bindings/Actions through the OutputRouter (completed in task 051) to create the rule-configured artifacts: `CreateEvent` → `sprk_event`, `CreateTask` → `task`, `CreateNotification` → `appnotification` (surfacing in Daily Briefing). REUSE the existing EventRules deterministic gates — cost cap, opt-out, explicit-command supersede, and the M4 confidence gate — do NOT reinvent them. Privilege is only **flagged**, never decided (ADR-015).

    Implement per the gate-050 boundary: consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` internals. The rule *configuration* (Binding rows + `sprk_matchconditions`) + tests are task 054; this task lands the firing + fan-out plumbing and reuse of the gates.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF/AI integration engineer. Authoritative on `EventRulesService.FireAsync`, the ordered Binding/Action fan-out, the `CreateEvent`/`CreateTask`/`CreateNotification` node executors, and the DailyBriefing notification path. Works within the r2-core-coordinated boundary + BFF hygiene governance.
  </role>

  <goal>
    An assessed communication (from `ICommunicationEnrichmentService`) fires `EventRulesService.FireAsync("communication_assessed")`; matching Bindings/Actions route through OutputRouter's now-complete `record`/`notification` legs to create `sprk_event` (CreateEvent), `task` (CreateTask), and `appnotification` (CreateNotification → Daily Briefing). All existing EventRules gates (cost cap, opt-out, explicit-command supersede, M4 confidence) are enforced (reused, not reimplemented); privilege is flagged only. Build clean; tests green; publish-size + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` clean; Placement Justification stated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-19: assessed communications feed Responsive Intelligence. Task 010 owns the enrichment pipeline (association → categorization → AI analysis → RAG → Responsive-Intelligence trigger). This task adds the trigger's fan-out via EventRules, reusing the existing deterministic gates so the new event source behaves like every other EventRules consumer. The best-effort/non-fatal invariant (NFR-06) MUST hold — fan-out failures do not fail enrichment or the send/inbound path.
    </background>
